      "text": "### Subrepresentations and Irreducibility"
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A **subrepresentation** (or G-invariant subspace) W ⊆ V satisfies: ρ(g)W ⊆ W for all g."
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#016",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A representation is **irreducible** (irrep) if it has no proper nonzero subrepresentations."
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#017",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Maschke's Theorem**: For G finite with char(k) ∤ |G| (e.g., k = ℂ always):\n```\nEvery representation V decomposes as a direct sum of irreducible representations.\nV = V₁^{m₁} ⊕ V₂^{m₂} ⊕ ... ⊕ Vₛ^{mₛ}"
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#018",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "mᵢ = multiplicity of Vᵢ in V.\nVᵢ are irreducible, and decomposition is unique (up to isomorphism).\n```"
    },
