        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Proof idea**: For any G-invariant subspace W ⊆ V, construct a G-equivariant projection P: V → W by averaging over G:\n```\nP = (1/|G|) Σ_{g∈G} ρ(g) ∘ P₀ ∘ ρ(g)⁻¹\n```\nwhere P₀ is any projection onto W. Then Im(P) = W and ker(P) is also G-invariant."
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#020",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
