        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Schur's Lemma**: The fundamental lemma of representation theory.\n```\nLet ρ: G → GL(V) and σ: G → GL(W) be irreps.\nLet φ: V → W be a G-equivariant map (intertwiner): φ∘ρ(g) = σ(g)∘φ."
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#021",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "(1) Either φ = 0 or φ is an isomorphism.\n(2) If V = W (same irrep) and k = ℂ: φ = λI for some λ ∈ ℂ."
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#022",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:24-representation-theory, git-history:mathematics:24-representation-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:representation-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Proof of (1): ker(φ) and Im(φ) are G-invariant subspaces → by irreducibility, each is 0 or all.\nProof of (2): φ has an eigenvalue λ (over ℂ). ker(φ - λI) is G-invariant → = V.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md#023",
      "path": [
        "24-REPRESENTATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
