        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[representation, theory]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Representation Theory - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Key facts:\n  Number of irreps = number of conjugacy classes.\n  Σᵢ (dim Vᵢ)² = |G|.\n  Rows are orthonormal under (1/|G|)Σ_C |C| · (row1)(row2)̄.\n  Columns are orthonormal under: (1/dim)Σ_ρ (dim ρ)(row of ρ at C₁)(row of ρ at C₂)̄.\n```"
    }
